<MainLayout
	title="About | Anticapitalist League Hungary"
	description="An introduction to the Anticapitalist League Hungary, an emerging civic and political initiative."
	lang="en"
	brandTone="navy"
>
	<header>
		<h1>About the League</h1>
		<p>
			The Anticapitalist League Hungary is an emerging political initiative seeking to
			rethink the foundations of an unsustainable economic, social, and cultural order.
			We see the crises of our time not merely as political or economic problems, but as
			expressions of a deeper spiritual disturbance in our relationship with life as a whole.
		</p>
		<p>
			Our aim is to move beyond capitalism on a spiritual foundation. We question a
			worldview that places material growth and profit above human dignity, community,
			and nature. Criticism alone is not enough: we seek an alternative from which
			fundamentally different answers to social, economic, and political questions can emerge.
		</p>
		<p>
			We understand the person as more than an isolated individual or an economic unit.
			Human life flourishes through responsibility, mutual respect, culture, and belonging
			to living communities. We value community self-determination and seek a society in
			which people, communities, and nature sustain one another.
		</p>
		<p>
			Nature is not merely a resource to be exploited: its protection takes precedence
			over economic interests. The economy should serve life and communities, not the
			other way around. Local economies and meaningful work have an important place in
			this vision, as does respect for the sacredness of life.
		</p>
		<p>
			The League's Constitution sets out its principles; the Guidelines connect them to
			the development of future programs. The Premodern Manifesto provides further
			spiritual background and questions assumptions of modernity and material progress.
			Our program outline remains a work in progress, open to discussion as our community
			and ideas take shape.
		</p>
		<p>
			This website shares our ideas and offers space for essays, literature, conversations,
			and news. We invite others to join a process of thought and participation that can
			help prepare the way towards a different future.
		</p>
	</header>
</MainLayout>
